notes: "When I talk to an agent about my slides, I used to say: fix slide four. But if the order changed since the last version, slide four is a different slide. So HUANDENG separates the two. Position is just where a slide sits now. The Slide ID is a short four-character code, letters and numbers, that belongs to the slide for good. This happened while I was preparing this talk: I added the acknowledgments slide near the end, and the closing slide moved from Position 25 to 26. Its Slide ID stayed SMGE. Now I can say: change the commands on SMGE, and the agent knows exactly which page I mean, next week as well as today. The same ID is what page history hangs on."
